<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rhoecus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">6th century BCE</span> · Also known as Rhoikos</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rhoecus was a Greek architect and sculptor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samo">Samos</a> in the sixth century BCE. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a> names him as the first architect of the great temple of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hera">Hera</a> at the Heraion, one of the first colossal Ionic temples, which he designed with Theodorus. Ancient tradition, recorded by Pliny and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pausanias-general">Pausanias</a>, credited the two with inventing the casting of bronze statues.</p></div>
